## Cloudflare Worker + `POST /upload`

Worker `projects/bbi-tf/workers/upload-proxy.js` forwards `upload.bbimarketing.com` → API Gateway `/upload` (must forward body + Basic Auth; **no 308**).

SST: `sst.config.ts` `POST /upload` → `src/http/upload/upload.handler`.

**ZIP name** (`parse-push-zip-filename.ts:20-21`):

```
[{uniqid}-]{store}_{YYYYMMDD}_{YYYYMMDD}_{HHMMSS}.zip
```

Not `…_da_….zip`. `_da_` is on **output tabs** (`:50-51`):

```
mmc_{store5}_{reportStart}_da_{reportEnd}_{extractTime}_MassMailCustInfo.tab
OR2_{store5}_{reportStart}_da_{reportEnd}_{extractTime}_OrdersDump.tab
```

Flow (`synthesize-push-zip.ts`): unzip require `CUS_*` + `OR2_*`; build MMC (late if delivery > threshold); upload both tabs; `file_list` insert `status: 1`, `ingested: false`, `legacy_ingested: false` (`:42-57` pattern via `insertFileListIfMissing`). Skip only if **both** MMC and OR2 rows exist; else regenerate.

nwk1 `pollingInfoRequest` still marks `pulse_version=4` when a matching zip exists under `/var/www/upload.bbimarketing.com/dominos-uploaded` (`new/api/index.php:682-712`) — keep that directory contract if dual-running.

## `mailing_addresses` + cohort SQL

Schema: `03-database-schema.mdc`. Ingest mapper `src/core/files/legacy-raw-mappers.ts` copies MMC street into `old_*` and `address` with `is_valid=0`.

Procedures (`docs/queries/report_procedures.sql`) — all join:

```
MassMail_RAW ⨝ mailing_addresses
  ON store_number AND old_address = Street
 AND pulse_profile_id = CustomerProfileID::text
 AND is_invalid = false
WHERE is_valid = 1
```

Windows: `p_start_date`/`p_end_date` converted with `AT TIME ZONE 'America/New_York'` because RAW epochs are ET wall-clock.

Join still requires `pulse_profile_id` so AccuZIP rows attach. After the join, cohort identity is the household `(store_number, address, zip5)`, not Pulse `CustomerProfileID`.

| Function | Rule |
|---|---|
| `get_new_customers` | New if `FirstOrderDate` is in the window and no `MassMail_RAW` at that address has `FirstOrderDate` in `[this FirstOrderDate − grace, this FirstOrderDate)`. Address match is PHP `LIKE`; K does not require the same Pulse profile. Grace default **180** days / `custom_stores.new_customer_grace` |
| `get_late_customers` | `LastLateOrderDate` in window, one row per household; `new_keys` exclusion uses the household New rule |
| `get_lapsed_customers` | PHP first-mail scan: last two `LastOrderDate`s on the certified household, calendar gap **28–180** days, `last + gap` inside the report window; skip New/Late this week. No `MassMail.lapsed` column. |

Used by `LegacyNllGenerateWorkflow`, HTTP `/api/stores/{store}/customers/{type}`, Slack slash commands. Do **not** write `NewCustomers`/`LateCustomers`/`LapsedCustomers` during AccuZIP apply.

## EC2 AccuZIP daemon + TaskToken

Repo `projects/bbi-accuzip-api`. **Live contract is SQS FIFO + WaitForTaskToken**, not HTTP `POST /exports`.

Step Functions (`address-validate.workflow.ts:156-167`):

```
WaitForAddressValidation
  queue AccuzipValidateQueue (FIFO)
  integration: token
  timeout: 7 days
  body: { downloadUrl, taskToken }
```

Daemon long-polls; downloads CSV to `{MAIL_DATA_SOURCE_ROOT}/postal_validate/API_MassMail_Export.csv`; AccuZIP writes `api_massmail_valid.txt`; watcher verifies write (MD5); uploads S3; `send_task_success(taskToken, {"validatedCsvUrl": "<presigned>"})` (`app/accuzip_sqs.py`). Timeout default 3h → `SendTaskFailure`. One `processing` job at a time.

Optional ops resume: `POST /api/workflows/address-validate/callback` (`SendTaskSuccessCommand`) — not the production path.

Resume: `ApplyPostalData` streams TSV, matches UK (`pulse_profile_id`, `store_number`, `old_*`), sets `address/city/state/zip5/crrt`, `is_valid=1`. Blank CRRT or errno `4.1`/`12.2`/`12.3` → `is_invalid=true` only if still unvalidated. Stamps watchdog `address_validated`.

```
NGP zip → CF Worker → POST /upload → S3 tabs + file_list
VPN stores → DownloadFileWorkflow Map → same
        → LegacyIngestWorkflow → MassMail_RAW / OR2_Raw + mailing_addresses
        → AddressValidateWorkflow → SQS token → AccuZIP NAS → ApplyPostalData
        → optional LegacyNllGenerateWorkflow (SQL cohorts)
```

When editing ingest or AccuZIP apply, keep `projects/nwk1/.../new/` polling UI (`pollingStatus` / `pollingList`) in mind: it still reads **apollo MySQL flags**, not Step Functions, unless `/sys/` SST UI is the target.
